ane</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Medical school faculty discontent: prevalence and predictors of intent to leave academic careers</article-title><source>BMC Med Educ</source><year>2007</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>37</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17935631</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1472-6920-7-37</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lambert</surname><given-names>TW</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldacre</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Views of doctors in training on the importance and availability of career advice in UK medicine</article-title><source>Med Educ</source><year>2007</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>460</fpage><lpage>466</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17470075</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1365-2929.2006.02675.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>O'Brodovich</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Beyene</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Tallett</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>MacGregor</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenblum</surname><given-names>ND</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Performance of a career development and compensation program at an Academic Health Science Center</article-title><source>Pediatrics</source><year>2007</year><volume>119</volume><fpage>e791</fpage><lpage>e797</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17339386</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1542/peds.2006-2207</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cooke</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Hurlock</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></pe